                <pb facs="0983" n="863" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg863"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Graves to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-10-18"><hi rendition="#italic">October 18,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the special
                    session of the Swedish Riksdag, which was called to consider the dissolution of
                    the union of Sweden and Norway, completed its labors and adjourned this day.</p>
                <p>The historical importance of the session caused the King to hold a formal and
                    ceremonious reception of the Riksdag in the throne room of the palace. Preceded
                    by the same elaborate ceremonial as is observed on the opening of annual
                    sessions of the Riksdag, and in presence of the royal family, the Duke and
                    Duchess of Connaught of England, all officers of the State, and the diplomatic
                    corps, King Oscar delivered an impressive and touching address to the Riksdag, a
                    copy and translation of which is herewith transmitted.</p>
                <p>This historical event marks the dissolution of the century-old union between the
                    nations of Sweden and Norway.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles H.
                    Graves.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d948-a1.xml" xpointer="d948-a1"/>
